import StackExchange.Puzzling139335.N4Axial.HorizontalReflection
import StackExchange.Puzzling139335.N4Axial.EqualRows

/-!
# Axial middle congruences in the reflected outer-pair configuration

Vertical translations and reflections in horizontal lines cannot exchange
the middle pieces when the center is protected. The arguments use the actual
four-piece density identity and compactness; they do not require the middle
union to be a Jordan region.

If both middle placements meet the right side, equal first matrix rows force
equal horizontal offsets. Their relative isometry is then one of the excluded
axial maps. A single right-contact point for each piece suffices.
-/
